# Trivy ignore file
#
# All CVEs below require upgrading to Spring Boot 3.x / Spring Framework 6.x.
# The project uses Spring Boot 2.7.18 (the version provided in the assessment
# skeleton). Upgrading to Spring Boot 3 requires Java 17+ and javax->jakarta
# package migration — outside the scope of this DevOps assessment.
#
# Remediation path for production: migrate to Spring Boot 3.3.x.

# Spring Framework 5.x CVEs — fixed in Spring 6.x only
# HttpInvokerServiceExporter — not used in this app
CVE-2016-1000027
# URL parsing — fixed in 5.3.32+, but Spring Boot 2.7.18 pins 5.3.31
CVE-2024-22243
# URL parsing — fixed in 5.3.33+
CVE-2024-22259
# URL parsing — fixed in 5.3.34+
CVE-2024-22262
# Path traversal RouterFunctions — not used in this app
CVE-2024-38816
# Path traversal functional web — not used in this app
CVE-2024-38819
# Annotation detection — fixed in Spring 6.2.11 only
CVE-2025-41249

# Spring Boot 2.x CVEs — fixed in Spring Boot 3.x only
# EndpointRequest matcher — app doesn't use EndpointRequest.to()
CVE-2025-22235
# Session hijacking via predictable values — fixed in 3.5.14+
CVE-2026-40973

# Jackson CVEs — fixed in 2.18.8+ which requires Kotlin 1.8 (project uses 1.6)
# jackson-core async parser bypass
GHSA-r7wm-3cxj-wff9
# jackson-databind PolymorphicTypeValidator — app uses default typing disabled
CVE-2026-54512
# jackson-databind security bypass
CVE-2026-54513
# jackson-core StackOverflowError — fixed in 2.15.0 but BOM upgrade breaks Kotlin 1.6
CVE-2025-52999
